<title>UK: Texaco Netherlands increases run cuts to 12.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Texaco Netherlands increases run cuts to 12.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Texaco Netherlands said poor refining margins had forced it to increase crude run cuts to 12.5 percent at the Rotterdam refinery it shares with British Petroleum Co Plc.</p>
<p>Texaco controls 35 percent of the 400,000 barrel per day (bpd) Nerefco refinery complex which it shares with BP. The 12.5 percent cut is equivalent to a 17,500 bpd crude cut.</p>
<p>On Tuesday the company said it had cut runs by 10 percent due to bad margins.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8980</p>
</text>
